              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OSV.dev reports RUSTSEC-2026-0387 for crates.io package crypto-bigint at version 0.5.5: Multiple timing variability issues in operations intended to be constant-time. The advisory carries neither a CVSS vector nor a database severity, so QSI rates it low and preliminary until it is triaged. The advisory names no affected functions, so reachability was not determined. Triage the advisory; upgrade to a fixed version (0.7.6) if it applies. Advisory data comes from OSV.dev at the recorded time. The advisory has no severity rating. Reachability is judged from names, not a call graph: the affected functions the advisory lists against the identifiers in the audited product code, a Cargo feature it says is off by default against the audited manifests, the platforms it lists against the declared Rust targets. Indirect calls (traits, macros, other dependencies) are not followed."
